# The overview's worked example: state living on a wire.
#
# Each station names the file its box lives in and the function inside
# it. The bare form — `keep` — works too, and means the same thing when
# only one file defines that name.
#
# `total` sends its result back into its own second port, so the running
# sum is waiting there when the next value arrives. Nothing is stored in
# any box; the loop is the memory.
#
# The loop needs one value to start with. Deliver a zero to total.1
# before the first input, or the station never has both ports full and
# nothing ever runs.
#
# Fed 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, `seen` collects every running total: 1, 3, 6, 10,
# 15. The order they come back out in is not promised.

boxes = ../src/boxes/

station feed (boxes/029-demo-boxes.c:keep)
  in 0 - 0$
  out 0 - total.0

station total (boxes/029-demo-boxes.c:add)
  in 0 - feed.0
  in 1 - total.0
  out 0 - total.1
  out 0 - seen.0

station seen (boxes/029-demo-boxes.c:keep)
  out 0 - 0$
  in 0 - total.0
